♫ I wake up every morning.

00:00:18.348 --> 00:00:19.604
- I'd like to feel that
after all these years,

00:00:19.604 --> 00:00:21.965
I'm myself at every given point.

00:00:21.965 --> 00:00:22.808
When I'm onstage,

00:00:22.808 --> 00:00:24.186
that's Freddy Mercury.

00:00:24.186 --> 00:00:25.019
When I'm offstage,

00:00:25.019 --> 00:00:26.219
I'm Freddy Mercury.

00:00:26.219 --> 00:00:27.478
And that's the only way to be,

00:00:27.478 --> 00:00:28.311
I mean I don't,

00:00:28.311 --> 00:00:31.037
the days have gone where
I actually felt that

00:00:31.037 --> 00:00:31.930
when I was onstage,

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:34.257
when I came off I still
had to sort of portray

00:00:34.257 --> 00:00:37.285
that Freddy Mercury image
because of other people.

00:00:37.285 --> 00:00:38.220
I used to do that before

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.686
because you have to grow up
and you have to understand,

00:00:40.686 --> 00:00:43.365
you have to really come
to grips with success.

00:00:43.365 --> 00:00:46.718
And over the years I found
out that you can become

00:00:46.718 --> 00:00:49.489
a very, very lonely person
if you have to do that,

00:00:49.489 --> 00:00:51.906
and I'm not afraid when I come offstage

00:00:51.906 --> 00:00:53.849
to actually be myself.

00:00:53.849 --> 00:00:55.337
- So this is a message I've been hearing

00:00:55.337 --> 00:00:57.564
more and more and more on the channel

00:00:57.564 --> 00:00:58.602
from the famous entrepreneurs

00:00:58.602 --> 00:01:00.300
that I've been paying attention to,

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:01.298
and I think it's so important.

00:01:01.298 --> 00:01:02.817
I think you have to be yourself

00:01:02.817 --> 00:01:03.891
because everybody else is taken.

00:01:03.891 --> 00:01:05.435
You're not going to have success

00:01:05.435 --> 00:01:06.757
being a copy of somebody else.

00:01:06.757 --> 00:01:09.972
I remember watching a video of Jay-Z,

00:01:09.972 --> 00:01:12.984
Warren Buffet and the guy from Forbes.

00:01:12.984 --> 00:01:14.498
And he was asking Jay-Z,

00:01:14.498 --> 00:01:16.762
"Do you ever get intimidated
being around Warren Buffet

00:01:16.762 --> 00:01:18.709
"and being around these guys in suits?

00:01:18.709 --> 00:01:19.709
"You know, you walk into a boardroom,

00:01:19.709 --> 00:01:20.956
"you're from the streets,

00:01:20.956 --> 00:01:23.149
"do you ever get intimidated?"

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:24.383
And he's like, "No."

00:01:24.383 --> 00:01:25.439
They're like, "Why not?"

00:01:25.439 --> 00:01:27.350
And he said, "Because I'm myself.

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:29.796
"Wherever I go, I'm myself."

00:01:29.796 --> 00:01:32.480
And there's so much
confidence that that brings

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:36.056
when you're not trying
to be somebody else,

00:01:36.056 --> 00:01:37.996
that when you go into any situation,

00:01:37.996 --> 00:01:38.829
any room,

00:01:38.829 --> 00:01:42.001
whether it's super outside
your comfort zone or not,

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:44.287
that you have the confidence
that you are awesome

00:01:44.287 --> 00:01:46.711
and you bring that everywhere you go.

00:01:46.711 --> 00:01:48.580
And what often happens
when you're first trying

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:49.642
to discover yourself,

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:51.011
think at the start of any process,

00:01:51.011 --> 00:01:52.334
you look up to people,

00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:54.446
you model success, right?

00:01:54.446 --> 00:01:55.367
You learn from them,

00:01:55.367 --> 00:01:56.760
you want to be the next Steve Jobs

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:58.146
so you copy some of the things from him.

00:01:58.146 --> 00:01:59.597
At some point you have to figure out,

00:01:59.597 --> 00:02:02.587
okay, I'm going to not
be the next Steve Jobs

00:02:02.587 --> 00:02:04.043
but I'm going to be the best me

00:02:04.043 --> 00:02:05.265
and I'm going to pull different pieces

00:02:05.265 --> 00:02:06.390
to allow that to happen.

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:08.326
And when you start experimenting,

00:02:08.326 --> 00:02:10.600
a lot of times what happens
is you go backwards.

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:12.883
This is what happened actually
at that Trinidad salsa.

00:02:12.883 --> 00:02:14.265
You know, I'm encouraging
all my instructors

00:02:14.265 --> 00:02:16.078
that you need to discover yourself.

00:02:16.078 --> 00:02:17.530
This is how I teach it,

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:19.439
this is how you know,

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:20.903
somebody else may teach it.

00:02:20.903 --> 00:02:22.768
You have to teach the same
moves that come out in class,

00:02:22.768 --> 00:02:24.751
but the way you teach it,

00:02:24.751 --> 00:02:25.845
the stories you tell,

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:28.057
the energy and vibe that you
bring has to be different

00:02:28.057 --> 00:02:29.525
because you can't be me.

00:02:29.525 --> 00:02:32.000
You can have the same message if you want,

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.194
if that's something that you believe in,

00:02:33.194 --> 00:02:34.036
but even that,

00:02:34.036 --> 00:02:34.907
how you deliver it,

00:02:34.907 --> 00:02:35.794
how you execute it,

00:02:35.794 --> 00:02:38.078
the vibe you bring will be different.

00:02:38.078 --> 00:02:38.929
If you try to be me,

00:02:38.929 --> 00:02:39.923
you're always going to fail.

00:02:39.923 --> 00:02:43.428
You're always going to fall
short of what you can do

00:02:43.428 --> 00:02:45.067
because you're not
actually being yourself,

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:47.463
you're being a copy of somebody else.

00:02:47.463 --> 00:02:49.975
And so, at the start to
figure out what it is

00:02:49.975 --> 00:02:52.454
that you stand for and
your one word helps you

00:02:52.454 --> 00:02:53.530
with that process,

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:54.778
understand what you stand for,

00:02:54.778 --> 00:02:59.325
and then start applying some
ideas into your business,

00:02:59.325 --> 00:03:01.068
into your life.

00:03:01.068 --> 00:03:02.541
I want to add more believe to my life.

00:03:02.541 --> 00:03:03.805
What does that look like?

00:03:03.805 --> 00:03:05.365
What does that look like in my videos,

00:03:05.365 --> 00:03:07.295
what does that look like
in my relationships?

00:03:07.295 --> 00:03:08.848
And at the start it may not work.

00:03:08.848 --> 00:03:10.928
You may try something and it doesn't work.

00:03:10.928 --> 00:03:12.424
And you have to experiment

00:03:12.424 --> 00:03:15.618
and have the confidence and the
courage that you are awesome

00:03:15.618 --> 00:03:16.908
and you're going to figure it out,

00:03:16.908 --> 00:03:20.267
and that the only way
you are going to win,

00:03:20.267 --> 00:03:21.430
the only way,

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:23.737
the game that you're playing in life,

00:03:23.737 --> 00:03:24.779
in business,

00:03:24.779 --> 00:03:29.108
the only way you're going to
win is if you go all in on you.

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:31.870
On the awesomeness that is you,

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:34.528
believe that what you have inside you

00:03:34.528 --> 00:03:37.173
is special and amazing
and start applying it.

00:03:37.173 --> 00:03:41.340
Radical self expression in
whatever way that comes out.

00:03:42.591 --> 00:03:44.915
It's the only way you're going to win.

00:03:44.915 --> 00:03:47.115
Stop just trying to copy somebody else,

00:03:47.115 --> 00:03:48.653
go all in on you.

00:03:48.653 --> 00:03:50.743
So the question of the day today
is I'd love to hear a story

00:03:50.743 --> 00:03:53.268
